€ In the midst of heated conversation about the ecological crisis, there always seems to be someone making these kinds of points. This is â€˜green growthâ€™ thinking. It is promoted by leading multilateral organisations and is assumed in national and international policymaking, including the European Green Deal, IPCC reports, the Paris Agreement and most recently in the USâ€™ Inflation Reduction Act. You are also likely to come across green growth in your private quarrels; for many, it has become common sense.&nbsp; The green growth p...","[2] 23 Responses to Economicsâ€™ Biggest-ever Question (rwer.wordpress.com, Tue, 14 Jul 2026 10:12:48 +0000) - Economicsandthe Biophysical Limits to Economic Growth Edited by Edward Fullbrook and Jamie Morgan For over a century economics has loosely guided the global economyâ€™s national economies. Natural science tells us that the climate crisis has been both caused by the global economy and ultimately threatens its existence. Because that crisis is now in an accelerating phase [â€¦]","[3] How US renewable-energy growth persists despite federal policy uncertainty (resilience.org, Tue, 14 Jul 2026 08:00:51 +0000) - Despite recent shifts in federal energy policies, a Carbon Brief analysis shows that the US transition to renewable energy is continuing.","[4] Rediscovering the Handcart (solar.lowtechmagazine.com, Wed, 22 Apr 2026 00:00:00 +0000) - <div class=\"article-img \"> <figure data-imgstate=\"dither\"> <img src=\"https://solar.lowtechmagazine.com/2026/04/rediscovering-the-handcart/images/dithers/IMG_2725_dithered.png\" alt='Image: The handcart, equipped with a sail. Photo by Kris De Decker.' loading=\"lazy\"/></figure> <figcaption class=\"caption\"> Image: The handcart, equipped with a sail. Photo by Kris De Decker. </figcaption> </div> </div> <p>The human-powered handcart is the oldest of vehicles, and it will likely be the last one around in the future. Of all vehicles, it&rsquo;s the cheapest and least complex to build and